treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia,” hosted by 
Universitätsbibliothek Heidelberg. The work presents illustrations and 
descriptions of gold signet rings and bead seals from a tomb context at Thisbê, 
identifying one as the Ring of Nestor and treating it as a key specimen for 
understanding Minoan or Minoan-influenced afterlife beliefs. Evans links the 
ring’s complex iconography to interpretations of Aegean religion and funerary 
ideas and emphasizes its role within a sepulchral treasure.",
