Nestor, and compares its iconography, such as scenes featuring a female figure 
on a boat, altars, sacred trees, and baetyls, with similar Aegean Bronze Age 
artifacts. By including the Ring of Nestor, the chapter situates it within 
scholarly discourse on potential forgeries and contested artifacts.",
