OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING OF NESTOR’”).  
- The full text of **Evans 1925**.  

Because your acceptance criteria require **concrete enumeration** of the bezel 
motifs and detailed discussion of interpretive themes, the present evidence is 
insufficient to meet those criteria fully. To close the gap, the next research 
step would need direct access (e.g., via institutional subscriptions or PDF 
downloads) to:

- Pini, I. 1998, *The “Ring of Nestor”*,  
- Vlachopoulos, A. G. 2020, *The Ring of Nestor and the Quest for Authenticity* 
(Aegis 18, 223–252),  
- The Academia.edu paper *“Some Observations on the Iconography of the ‘Ring of 
Nestor’”*,  
- Marinatos & Jackson, *The Pseudo‑Minoan Nestor Ring and Its Egyptian 
Iconography* (JAEI 3.2, 17–27).  

Only those texts can supply the precise counts and arrangement of figures, the 
