- Pini, I. 1998, *The “Ring of Nestor”*,  
- Vlachopoulos, A. G. 2020, *The Ring of Nestor and the Quest for Authenticity* 
(Aegis 18, 223–252),  
- The Academia.edu paper *“Some Observations on the Iconography of the ‘Ring of 
Nestor’”*,  
- Marinatos & Jackson, *The Pseudo‑Minoan Nestor Ring and Its Egyptian 
Iconography* (JAEI 3.2, 17–27).  

Only those texts can supply the precise counts and arrangement of figures, the 
full set of animals, vegetation, and architectural motifs, and the detailed 
arguments on epiphany/cult versus other narrative readings.

