visible)  
- **URL:** https://ignca.gov.in/Asi_data/11774.pdf  
- **Publisher:** Indira Gandhi National Centre for the Arts (IGNCA – Indian 
governmental cultural institution)  
- **Author:** Not fully visible; likely part of an Archaeological Survey of 
India publication series  
- **Date:** Not visible in snippet  
- **Source type:** Government / archival PDF (likely a catalog or scholarly 
text)  
- **Query that triggered it:** `"Ring of Nestor" gold ring museum holdings 
Athens National Archaeological Museum Ashmolean -site:en.wikipedia.org`  

**Key snippet (as provided by search):**

> “Mycenaean Tree and Pillar Cult and 'The Ring of Nestor, etc., and reproduce 
... Gold ring in the National Museum, Athens. the Ashmolean Museum, Oxford ...”

**Observations:**

- The fragment indicates that the document discusses (or at least mentions) 
scholarship such as **Mycenaean Tree and Pillar Cult** and “The Ring of Nestor,”
and that it refers to:
  - A “Gold ring in the National Museum, Athens,” and  
  - “the Ashmolean Museum, Oxford …” (the phrase is cut off).  
- The context likely involves description of images reproduced from different 
museums (National Archaeological Museum, Athens; Ashmolean Museum, Oxford) and 
may be summarizing where certain objects or photographs are located.  
- It is not yet possible, from the snippet alone, to tell whether this is 
stating that **the same ring** (Ring of Nestor) is in both institutions (e.g., 
via casts, replicas, or loans) or whether different rings are being referenced 
in juxtaposition.

**Relevance:**

- Provides an **archival/scholarly lead** suggesting both **Athens National 
Museum** and **Ashmolean Museum, Oxford** appear in the same context involving 
“The Ring of Nestor” and Mycenaean tree/pillar cult studies.  
- Useful as a starting point to search within the PDF (locally, outside this 
