### 2. Athens National Archaeological Museum references (catalog identifiers)

#### 2.1 “Deconstructing a Narrative of Epiphany on the Isopata Ring” (journal 
article)

- **Title:** Deconstructing a Narrative of Epiphany on the Isopata Ring  
- **URL:** https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/pdfplus/10.2307/507325  
- **Publisher:** University of Chicago Press (Journal of Near Eastern Studies)  
- **Author:** Not fully visible in snippet; article about the Isopata Ring 
(Aegean archaeology and iconography)  
- **Date:** Not visible in snippet; older article (JNES, mid-late 20th century) 
- **Source type:** Peer-reviewed scholarly journal article  
- **Query that triggered it:** `"Ring of Nestor" "Athens National Museum" 1801 
CMS I 219`  

**Relevant sentence (from the snippet):**

> “The ring is in the Athens National Museum, no. 1801. See CMS I, no. 219 for 
publication data.”

**Context and relevance:**

- The article primarily discusses the **Isopata Ring**, but here it apparently 
refers to another ring (evidently the one also published in the **Corpus der 
Minoischen und Mykenischen Siegel** (CMS)) and states that:
  - The ring is in the **Athens National Museum** (i.e., National Archaeological
Museum in Athens).  
  - It has museum number **1801**.  
  - It appears in CMS I as **no. 219**.  
- This is an **explicit scholarly statement** linking a ring (in the context of 
Minoan/Mycenaean signet rings and epiphany scenes) to Athens National Museum 
inventory number **1801** and CMS I **219**. Given the query and the associated 
CMS citation, this is used in scholarship as a reference point for the ring 
frequently discussed as the “Ring of Nestor.”  
- The article itself does not (in the visible snippet) elaborate on provenance 
transfers or on Ashmolean holdings, but it affirms a museum number and catalog 
publication reference.

---

#### 2.2 Cambridge “Mycenaean Civilization – Figures and Sources of Photographs”

- **Title:** Figures and Sources of Photographs – Mycenaean Civilization  
- **URL:** 
https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/mycenaean-civilization/figures-and-sources-
of-photographs/D6D37305091C366AC39E9CF1C121CCF4  
