Egyptian prototypes, highlighting a butterfly motif as especially significant. 
The authors argue that this butterfly and other elements form a semantically 
coherent Egyptian-style iconographic program, and use this coherence to question
the ring’s authenticity, suggesting that the composition may be a modern 
