    {
      "local_ref": "e15",
      "text": "Hudler synthesizes that the guardian creature motif (interpreted 
as dog, dragon or scorpion), the central tree, altars, figure poses, and overall
compositional layout are repeatedly treated in the literature as key 
iconographic features for judging the Ring of Nestor’s authenticity.",
      "document_ref": "d4",
      "source_ref": "s4",
      "evidence_type": "other",
      "locator": null,
