- **Title**: Search – Ashmolean Museum Image Library  
- **URL**: https://images.ashmolean.org/search/?searchQuery=%20nestor  
- **Publisher / Author**: Ashmolean Museum, University of Oxford  
- **Date**: Not stated on search results page; the entry is a static collection 
catalogue record (access date not applicable here, but page reflects modern 
cataloguing practice).  
- **Source type**: Museum collection catalogue / image library  
- **Triggered by query**: `"Ring of Nestor" Ashmolean AN1938.1130 National 
Archaeological Museum Athens 1801 CMS I 219`  

- **Relevance to the research question**:  
  The Ashmolean image library provides the primary, authoritative catalogue 
record for the Oxford ring, confirming its accession number (AN1938.1130), 
descriptive title (“Signet ring”), popular name (“The Ring of Nestor”), period 
(Late Minoan I), and that the ring is currently held by the Ashmolean. It is 
crucial for distinguishing the Ashmolean “Ring of Nestor” from the Mycenae ring 
in Athens and for confirming that the Oxford ring exists as a distinct, 
catalogued artifact. It does not, however, mention any connection with the 
National Archaeological Museum in Athens or with an inventory number NAM 1801 / 
CMS I, 219.  

- **Content / faithful summary**:  
  The Ashmolean search results page lists an entry for “AN1938.1130” described 
as a “Signet ring” with the “preferred (descriptive)” title and a “popular 
(original language)” name “The Ring of Nestor”, dated to the “Late Minoan I 
Period (c. 1600 – c. 1450 BC).” The entry is part of the museum’s online image 
library, which offers images for licensing and provides succinct catalogue data:
object type (signet ring), material (gold, implied in related stock-image 
descriptions), date/period (Late Minoan I), and descriptive/popular titles. The 
search interface shows that this is a standard collection item within the 
Ashmolean’s holdings; there is no indication of it being on loan from another 
institution or deaccessioned to another museum. No mention is made of the 
National Archaeological Museum, Athens, or of any catalogue number other than 
AN1938.1130.  

